  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HCFC phase-out management plan (stage III)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The HCFC Phase out Management Plan (HPMP) Stage III is a sector-wide programme designed to help Mexico gradually reduce their use of hydrochlorofluorocarbons (HCFCs), which destroys the earth#s protective ozone layer and contributes to global greenhouse gas emissions. The activities planned for the HPMP Stage III include initiatives to phase out HCFC-22 in the servicing sector in Mexico, HPMP coordination, monitoring of HCFC production and public awareness raising in Mexico.</narrative>
  </description>
